*  PUT_driver - exercises PUT(L): output L with a label starting in column
*  73, the label taken from the variable PUT_LABEL, the lines numbered in
*  increments of 1 unless PUT_INC says otherwise.  Contract per PUT.sno
*  header.  Cases: the default numbering, a label set by the caller, an
*  increment other than 1, a line long enough to reach toward column 73, and
*  the null line.
-INCLUDE "PUT.sno"
        PUT('first line')
        PUT('second line')
        PUT_LABEL  =  'TAG'
        PUT('after the label was set')
        PUT_INC  =  10
        PUT('after the increment was set')
        PUT('and again')
        PUT('a much longer line of text that runs on for a while')
        PUT()
END
